  <section class="page">
    <article class="content-block">
      <h2>Next Up and playlist synchronization</h2>
      <p>For builds with native Jellyfin lists, see the <a href="https://github.com/eslutz/A-Playa-Named-Gus/wiki/Next-Up-and-Playlists">Next Up, Playlists and Collections guide</a>. Jellyfin owns playlist and collection names, membership, playlist order and permissions. Gus caches lists by server/user and saves offline edits until it can contact Jellyfin. Collections group titles; all-video playlists support ordered video playback, existing audio playlists open the audio player, and mixed-media entries open individually.</p>
      <p>Home Next Up sorts by recent activity. Optional private iCloud synchronization carries Gus resume positions, Next Up intent and activity; it requires the same iCloud account and independent sign-in to the same Jellyfin server/user on each device. Native lists come from Jellyfin, pending server edits stay on their originating device, and downloaded files remain device-local. Previous Gus playlists can be explicitly imported with originals preserved. Jellyfin 10.11.11 accepts each media item once per playlist, so legacy lists with repeated items are preserved and import reports a limitation instead of silently collapsing entries.</p>
      <p>If a server change needs review, refresh and inspect Jellyfin before explicitly retrying or discarding it: a create/add request may have succeeded even when its response was lost. A missing video-playlist item can be retried, skipped, or explicitly replaced without deleting your underlying media. Signed iCloud provisioning and physical cross-device validation remain pending for this feature branch.</p>
    </article>
